Testing
Makefile
# ...but tests/host/Makefile is hand-written and has to be in the repository:
# the CI host-tests job is just `make -C tests/host`, which fails with "No
# targets specified and no makefile found" on a fresh clone if this is ignored.
# The pattern above is unanchored, so it matched at every depth. CMake's own
# generated Makefiles live under build/, which `**/build/` already excludes.
!tests/host/Makefile
